# Docs and change control

## Do

- Update `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/security.md` when boundaries or threat model change.
- Update `docs/ai-workflow/` indexes when adding rules, commands, or skills.
- Keep `.cursor/skills/` and `.claude/skills/` content identical per skill name.
- Document security tradeoffs and known limitations in `docs/security.md`.
- Reference official docs (VS Code API, Cursor hooks/MCP, Telegram Bot API, MCP spec) in guides.

## Do not

- Claim features work in README before implementation exists.
- Commit real tokens in docs, examples, or `mcp.json`.
- Leave broken links from README to missing docs.

## PR expectations

Describe security impact, Telegram/MCP surface changes, and whether hook policy defaults changed.
